ontent":"uniku is ESM-only. Import the exact generator you want rather than a package-root barrel:"},"131":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-7","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#install","content":"For a Deno project without a package import map, use Deno's npm specifier directly:"},"132":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-8","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#the-usual-shape","content":"The named generator import has two roles. Call it to generate an ID. Use the same value as a dictionary of methods and constants for that strategy."},"133":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-9","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#the-usual-shape","content":"If you are used to class APIs, the attached helpers resemble \"static methods.\" The generator is still a function, so there is nothing to instantiate:"},"134":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-10","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#the-usual-shape","content":"You do not import `toBytes()` or `timestamp()` separately. They stay attached to `uuidv7` and grouped with that strategy."},"135":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-11","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#the-usual-shape","content":"Every generator value exposes `isValid()`. The remaining API matches the strategy. Time-ordered formats expose `timestamp()`. Formats with a canonical binary representation expose `toBytes()` and `fromBytes()`. CUID v2 and Nanoid expose a smaller API because they have no canonical byte representation. UUID v5 is the one generator that takes an input: it derives the same ID from the same name and namespace, and adds `namespace()` plus the RFC 9562 namespace constants."},"136":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#the-usual-shape","content":"Each generator reference lists the exact call signatures, methods, constants, and overloads available from its imported value."},"137":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Each format is independently importable and tree-shakeable. Install one package, then ship only the strategy your application imports."},"138":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Strategy"},"139":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-15","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Direct import"},"140":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-16","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Usual function call"},"141":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-17","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"Primary value"},"142":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"UUID v4"},"143":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-19","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"`uniku/uuid/v4`"},"144":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-20","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"`uuidv4()`"},"145":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-21","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"`string`"},"146":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-22","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started#every-strategy","content":"UUID v5"},"147":{"id":"/docs/getting-started-23","page_id":"/docs/getting-started","t